      "senderName": "NWS Great Falls MT",
      "headline": "Winter Storm Warning issued October 10 at 4:13PM MDT until October 12 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Great Falls MT",
      "description": "* WHAT...Heavy, wet snow expected. Total snow accumulations between 7\nand 14 inches. Winds gusting as high as 35 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Meagher County Valleys, Cascade County below 5000ft,\nEastern Pondera and Eastern Teton, and Judith Basin County and\nJudith Gap.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 AM MDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult. Gusty winds combined with\nthe wet and heavy nature of the snow could bring down tree\nbranches. Isolated power outages are possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Snowfall amounts will vary drastically from\ngrassy surfaces to roadways, most notably at lower elevations, with\naccumulations on non-grassy surfaces being confined mainly to\nbetween the evening through late morning hours.",
      "instruction": "If you must travel, keep an extra flashlight, food, and water in your\nvehicle in case of an emergency. The latest road conditions for the\nstate you are calling from can be obtained by calling 5 1 1.",
